Subject: Make a YUV ColorBuffer linear so no driver keeps its pictures compressed

What a guest CPU writes into a YUV buffer (a video's pictures, a camera's frames) reaches its
ColorBuffer through a copy into the ColorBuffer's image, and SurfaceFlinger samples it through
an image of its own on the same memory, made on the guest's VkDevice. Both images were
optimal. On the owner's PC (Intel Arc, 0.2.4-dev.15, with patches 0030 and 0031) a YouTube
video still showed blocks of light purple and yellow-green in the flat areas near the top left
of its picture, intermittently, while the detailed rest of the picture was right; the host's
hardware decoder and the guest's software decoder gave the same blocks, and the decoder's
planes were checked whole. Wrong chroma in blocks, only where the picture is flat, is what a
compressed surface read as uncompressed looks like: flat blocks compress, detailed ones do not.
0031 released the copied image to the external queue family, but the guest takes its image
from there once, when SurfaceFlinger first imports the buffer (from VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED,
as ANGLE does for an AHardwareBuffer), not after each copy, so the pair is never complete for
the pictures that follow.

Now a device-local ColorBuffer of VK_FORMAT_G8_B8R8_2PLANE_420_UNORM or
VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM is linear whenever the device samples it through the 4:2:0
conversion (midpoint chroma), copies it both ways and exports it in linear tiling, and the image
a guest makes to import such a buffer is made linear too, since an image that reads the
ColorBuffer's memory must be made as the ColorBuffer's image was. A linear image is never
compressed, so every reader sees the planes as they were written. A device that cannot keeps
optimal ColorBuffers, and the renderer says so once per format; on one that can it says that
YUV ColorBuffers are linear. RGB ColorBuffers, which the GPU draws, stay optimal.

diff --git a/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.cpp b/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.cpp
--- a/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.cpp
+++ b/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 
 #include <chrono>
 #include <iomanip>
+#include <mutex>
 #include <ostream>
 #include <sstream>
 #include <thread>
@@ -3278,7 +3279,7 @@
 
     VkImageTiling tiling = (infoPtr->memoryProperty & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT)
                                ? VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR
-                               : VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL;
+                               : colorBufferTiling(vkFormat);
     std::unique_ptr<VkImageCreateInfo> imageCi = generateColorBufferVkImageCreateInfoLocked(
         vkFormat, infoPtr->width, infoPtr->height, tiling);
     // pNext will be filled later.
@@ -3539,6 +3540,59 @@
         written = written || supportInfo.usageFlags == VK_IMAGE_USAGE_TRANSFER_DST_BIT;
     }
     return sampled && written;
+}
+
+VkImageTiling VkEmulation::colorBufferTiling(VkFormat format) const {
+    // A YUV ColorBuffer holds what a guest CPU wrote (a video's pictures, a camera's
+    // frames): the host copies the planes in, and the guest samples them through an image of
+    // its own on the same memory, made on another VkDevice. A driver that compresses an
+    // optimal image (Intel Arc) left flat areas of the copied picture compressed, and the
+    // guest's image read the compressed blocks as they lie in memory: a YouTube video showed
+    // blocks of light purple and yellow-green in its flat areas, intermittently, with the
+    // host's hardware decoder and the guest's software decoder alike, while the detailed
+    // rest of the picture was right. Releasing the image to the external queue family did
+    // not stop it, since the guest takes the image from there once and never again. A linear
+    // image is never compressed, so every reader sees the planes as written.
+    if (format != VK_FORMAT_G8_B8R8_2PLANE_420_UNORM &&
+        format != VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM) {
+        return VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL;
+    }
+    // Sampled through the 4:2:0 conversion the ColorBuffer's view and the guest use, written
+    // and read back by copies, as a 2D linear image with the external memory every
+    // ColorBuffer is made with where the device exports memory.
+    constexpr VkFormatFeatureFlags kNeeded =
+        VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_BIT | VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_MIDPOINT_CHROMA_SAMPLES_BIT |
+        VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_TRANSFER_SRC_BIT | VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_TRANSFER_DST_BIT;
+    bool sampled = false;
+    bool written = false;
+    bool read = false;
+    for (const auto& supportInfo : mImageSupportInfo) {
+        if (supportInfo.format != format || !supportInfo.supported ||
+            supportInfo.type != VK_IMAGE_TYPE_2D ||
+            supportInfo.tiling != VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR ||
+            (supportInfo.formatProps2.formatProperties.linearTilingFeatures & kNeeded) !=
+                kNeeded ||
+            (mDeviceInfo.supportsExternalMemoryExport && !supportInfo.supportsExternalMemory)) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        sampled = sampled || supportInfo.usageFlags == VK_IMAGE_USAGE_SAMPLED_BIT;
+        written = written || supportInfo.usageFlags == VK_IMAGE_USAGE_TRANSFER_DST_BIT;
+        read = read || supportInfo.usageFlags == VK_IMAGE_USAGE_TRANSFER_SRC_BIT;
+    }
+    const bool linear = sampled && written && read;
+    static std::once_flag sLogged[2];
+    std::call_once(sLogged[format == VK_FORMAT_G8_B8R8_2PLANE_420_UNORM ? 0 : 1], [&] {
+        if (linear) {
+            INFO("YUV ColorBuffers of %s are linear: no driver compresses what is copied in.",
+                 string_VkFormat(format));
+        } else {
+            WARN("YUV ColorBuffers of %s are optimal: this device cannot sample, copy and "
+                 "export them linear, so a driver that compresses them may show blocks in a "
+                 "video's flat areas.",
+                 string_VkFormat(format));
+        }
+    });
+    return linear ? VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR : VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL;
 }
 
 bool VkEmulation::isFormatSupported(GLenum format) {
diff --git a/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.h b/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.h
--- a/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.h
+++ b/host/vulkan/VkCommonOperations.h
@@ -255,6 +255,11 @@
